{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1533353177,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNDc1ODIyMDc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2737","origin":"github"},"title":"FOI: publish --to=cache must avoid merging/pushing that remote's git-annex","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nWith #2668 we can now get efficient caching etc.  But as discussed in http://git-annex.branchable.com/tips/local_caching_of_annexed_files we must not fetch or `annex merge` it.  So whenever we would \"publish\" to such a remote we must avoid doing anything what we typically do (fetch/merge/sync) for publishing to make it succeed.  So we should consult git settings for that remote and avoid doing those operations.","files":null}]}